  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(\\frac{2}{3})=41.810{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{41.81}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${41.81}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={41.81}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={41.81}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={41.81}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977985/assets/bc0c031fe6ccbb40dc77474582b301456f537ee2a649ba2d5b3bca9b1240618f.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}-{41.81}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={138.19}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are $x={42}^{\u2218},{138}^{\u2218}.$",
